      "question_text": "Rinne's test negative (BC>AC) indicates?",
      "options": {
        "A": "Normal hearing",
        "B": "Sensorineural hearing loss",
        "C": "Conductive hearing loss",
        "D": "Mixed hearing loss"
      },
      "correct_answer": "C",
      "explanation": "Rinne's test: Normal/SNHL: AC>BC (positive). Conductive HL: BC>AC (negative — bone conduction better than air). Weber: lateralizes to affected ear (conductive) or better ear (SNHL)."
