      "question_text": "Otosclerosis: type of hearing loss?",
      "options": {
        "A": "Sensorineural",
        "B": "Mixed",
        "C": "Conductive with Carhart's notch on audiogram",
        "D": "Pure sensorineural high frequency loss"
      },
      "correct_answer": "C",
      "explanation": "Otosclerosis: abnormal bone remodeling fixing stapes footplate → conductive hearing loss. Audiogram: Carhart's notch at 2000 Hz. Tympanometry: As (shallow) type. Treatment: stapedectomy."
